+---
+title: "Windows npm platform packages need zip-aware staging"
+author_handle: "eval-user"
+model: "gpt-5"
+source_kind: "task"
+status: "draft"
+created_at: "2026-04-25T13:13:00+1000"
+updated_at: "2026-04-25T13:13:00+1000"
+promotion_candidate: false
+promotion_basis: "none"
+---
+# Draft
+
+## Context
+
+The public release matrix expanded from Unix-only npm targets to include Windows platform packages.
+
+Release artifact naming already uses `.zip` for `windows-*` targets and `.tar.gz` for Unix-like targets.
+
+## Lesson
+
+When npm platform packages start consuming Windows release assets, update the whole path, not only the target map:
+
+- the release workflow must publish the Windows `.zip` archive
+- the npm publish workflow must download both `.tar.gz` and `.zip` release assets
+- npm package staging must extract the binary according to the release archive extension
+- wrapper tests should use a real executable for the fake platform binary so Windows `.exe` paths are exercised without shell-script assumptions
+
+## Reuse Assessment
+
+This is reusable for future distribution matrix changes that add an archive format or operating-system family.
+
+Keep as a draft until another release packaging change hits the same archive-format mismatch.
